    "question_hi": "What is blocking vs non-blocking code?",
    "answer_hi": "**Blocking code** halts the execution of further JavaScript until an operation completes (synchronous operations like `fs.readFileSync()`). It blocks the single main thread, freezing all other incoming requests.\n\n**Non-blocking code** delegates the time-consuming operation (such as file reads, network calls, or database queries) to the OS or libuv, allowing the main thread to immediately continue executing subsequent code. Once the operation finishes, its callback or Promise is placed in the event loop queue.",
