    "answer_hi": "A callback is a function passed as an argument to another function, which is intended to be called back later once an asynchronous task completes.\n\n```javascript\nconst fs = require('fs');\n\nfs.readFile('example.txt', 'utf8', (err, data) => {\n  if (err) return console.error(err);\n  console.log(data);\n});\n```\n\nIn Node.js, the convention is error-first callbacks: the first parameter is reserved for an error object (or `null` if successful), and subsequent parameters hold the result.",
