    "question_hi": "What is package.json and npm in detail?",
    "answer_hi": "package.json is an important file in a Node.js project. It contains project information, dependencies, scripts, and other configuration. npm stands for Node Package Manager. We use it to install and manage packages such as Express, mysql2, and dotenv. The dependencies section lists packages required by the application, while devDependencies lists packages mainly needed during development. We can also define scripts to run common commands. The package-lock.json file records the resolved dependency versions to help keep installations consistent.\n\nCommon commands:\n```bash\nnpm init -y\nnpm install express\nnpm install --save-dev nodemon\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nExample script inside package.json:\n```json\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"start\": \"node app.js\",\n    \"dev\": \"nodemon app.js\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nRemember: package.json describes the project and its packages; npm installs and manages them.",
