    "question_hi": "What is process.nextTick()?",
    "answer_hi": "`process.nextTick()` schedules a callback to run immediately after the current operation completes, before the event loop continues to its next phase or processes any I/O callbacks. It is executed before microtasks and before `setImmediate()`. Because it runs before the event loop proceeds, calling it recursively can starve the event loop of I/O.",
