    "category": "A. Node.js Fundamentals (1–30)",
    "question_hi": "What is the difference between setTimeout() and setImmediate()?",
    "answer_hi": "Both schedule asynchronous callbacks:\n- **`setTimeout(fn, 0)`:** Schedules a callback to run in the **Timers** phase after a minimum delay of 1ms has elapsed.\n- **`setImmediate(fn)`:** Schedules a callback to run in the **Check** phase of the event loop, immediately after the I/O polling phase.\n\nInside an I/O cycle (like inside `fs.readFile`), `setImmediate` is guaranteed to always run before `setTimeout(fn, 0)`.",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between setTimeout() and setImmediate()?",
    "answer_en": "Both schedule asynchronous callbacks:\n- **`setTimeout(fn, 0)`:** Schedules a callback to run in the **Timers** phase after a minimum delay of 1ms has elapsed.\n- **`setImmediate(fn)`:** Schedules a callback to run in the **Check** phase of the event loop, immediately after the I/O polling phase.\n\nInside an I/O cycle (like inside `fs.readFile`), `setImmediate` is guaranteed to always run before `setTimeout(fn, 0)`.",
