    "answer_hi": "A Buffer is a global class in Node.js used to handle raw binary data directly in memory. Since JavaScript initially only handled strings, Buffer was introduced to represent fixed-length sequences of bytes outside the V8 heap. Buffers are used when dealing with TCP streams, reading image/video files, and handling encrypted network packets.",
