    "category": "A. Node.js Fundamentals (1–30)",
    "question_hi": "What is EventEmitter in Node.js?",
    "answer_hi": "EventEmitter is a core class from the `events` module that enables the publisher-subscriber (Pub/Sub) pattern in Node.js. Many core modules (like HTTP servers and streams) inherit from EventEmitter.\n\n```javascript\nconst EventEmitter = require('events');\nconst emitter = new EventEmitter();\n\n// Listener\nemitter.on('userLoggedIn', (user) => {\n  console.log(`Welcome, ${user.name}`);\n});\n\n// Trigger event\nemitter.emit('userLoggedIn', { name: 'Aditi' });\n```",
    "question_en": "What is EventEmitter in Node.js?",
    "answer_en": "EventEmitter is a core class from the `events` module that enables the publisher-subscriber (Pub/Sub) pattern in Node.js. Many core modules (like HTTP servers and streams) inherit from EventEmitter.\n\n```javascript\nconst EventEmitter = require('events');\nconst emitter = new EventEmitter();\n\n// Listener\nemitter.on('userLoggedIn', (user) => {\n  console.log(`Welcome, ${user.name}`);\n});\n\n// Trigger event\nemitter.emit('userLoggedIn', { name: 'Aditi' });\n```",
    "source": "written",
