    "question_hi": "What is Express.js and why do we use it?",
    "answer_hi": "Express.js is a minimal, fast, and flexible web application framework for Node.js. While Node's core `http` module allows building web servers, it requires manual parsing of URLs, routing, request bodies, and headers. Express provides a robust set of features including intuitive routing, middleware pipelines, template engine integration, and simplified HTTP utility methods like `res.json()`.",
