    "num": "33",
    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "How do you create custom middleware in Express?",
    "answer_hi": "A custom middleware is simply a function with `(req, res, next)`. You can inspect headers, validate authentication, log metrics, or attach helper properties to `req`:\n\n```javascript\nconst checkAdmin = (req, res, next) => {\n  if (req.headers['x-role'] === 'admin') {\n    next(); // proceed\n  } else {\n    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied: Admin only' });\n  }\n};\n\napp.get('/admin/dashboard', checkAdmin, (req, res) => {\n  res.json({ message: 'Welcome to admin panel' });\n});\n```",
    "question_en": "How do you create custom middleware in Express?",
    "answer_en": "A custom middleware is simply a function with `(req, res, next)`. You can inspect headers, validate authentication, log metrics, or attach helper properties to `req`:\n\n```javascript\nconst checkAdmin = (req, res, next) => {\n  if (req.headers['x-role'] === 'admin') {\n    next(); // proceed\n  } else {\n    res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied: Admin only' });\n  }\n};\n\napp.get('/admin/dashboard', checkAdmin, (req, res) => {\n  res.json({ message: 'Welcome to admin panel' });\n});\n```",
    "source": "written",
    "topic": "node"
