    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "What is the difference between app.use() and app.get()?",
    "answer_hi": "- **`app.use([path], middleware)`:** Mounts middleware functions for **all** HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) that match the path prefix. It is used for global tasks like parsing bodies, setting CORS, logging, or sub-routers.\n- **`app.get(path, handler)`:** Handles **only** incoming HTTP GET requests that match the exact specified route path.",
