    "num": "36",
    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "What are req.params, req.query, and req.body?",
    "answer_hi": "In Express, req.params, req.query, and req.body are used to get data from an incoming request, but they get it from different places. req.params gets values from the URL path. For example, in /users/10, the user ID is available through req.params.id. req.query gets values from the query string. For example, in /users?city=Lucknow, the city is available through req.query.city. req.body gets data sent inside the request body, usually when creating or updating records. We need middleware like express.json() to read JSON request bodies. These three are important because APIs need to receive information from the frontend. We should also validate the received data before using it in database queries.\n\n```javascript\napp.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {\n  res.json({\n    id: req.params.id,\n    city: req.query.city\n  });\n});\n```\n\nRemember: Params = URL path, query = URL filters, body = sent data.",
    "question_en": "What are req.params, req.query, and req.body?",
    "answer_en": "In Express, req.params, req.query, and req.body are used to get data from an incoming request, but they get it from different places. req.params gets values from the URL path. For example, in /users/10, the user ID is available through req.params.id. req.query gets values from the query string. For example, in /users?city=Lucknow, the city is available through req.query.city. req.body gets data sent inside the request body, usually when creating or updating records. We need middleware like express.json() to read JSON request bodies. These three are important because APIs need to receive information from the frontend. We should also validate the received data before using it in database queries.\n\n```javascript\napp.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {\n  res.json({\n    id: req.params.id,\n    city: req.query.city\n  });\n});\n```\n\nRemember: Params = URL path, query = URL filters, body = sent data.",
