    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "What are HTTP methods: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, and DELETE?",
    "answer_hi": "- **GET:** Retrieves data from the server (idempotent, safe, no body).\n- **POST:** Submits new data to create a new resource on the server.\n- **PUT:** Replaces the target resource entirely with the request payload.\n- **PATCH:** Partially updates specific fields of an existing resource.\n- **DELETE:** Removes the specified resource from the server.",
