    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "What is the difference between res.send() and res.json()?",
    "answer_hi": "- **`res.send()`:** Automatically inspects the payload and sets the `Content-Type` header (e.g., `text/html` for strings, `application/json` for objects, `application/octet-stream` for Buffers).\n- **`res.json()`:** Explicitly sets `Content-Type: application/json` and converts objects, arrays, nulls, and booleans into valid JSON using `JSON.stringify()`. For building REST APIs, `res.json()` is preferred for consistency.",
    "question_en": "What is the difference between res.send() and res.json()?",
