    "num": "42",
    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "What is express.json() and why is it needed?",
    "answer_hi": "`express.json()` is a built-in middleware in Express based on `body-parser`. When a client sends an HTTP request with a JSON body and `Content-Type: application/json`, Node receives it as a raw stream of data chunks. `express.json()` buffers the chunks, parses them into a JavaScript object, and attaches it to `req.body`. Without it, `req.body` will be `undefined`.",
    "question_en": "What is express.json() and why is it needed?",
    "answer_en": "`express.json()` is a built-in middleware in Express based on `body-parser`. When a client sends an HTTP request with a JSON body and `Content-Type: application/json`, Node receives it as a raw stream of data chunks. `express.json()` buffers the chunks, parses them into a JavaScript object, and attaches it to `req.body`. Without it, `req.body` will be `undefined`.",
