    "num": "44",
    "category": "B. Express.js Core (31–45)",
    "question_hi": "How do you handle 404 (Not Found) errors in Express?",
    "answer_hi": "In Express, 404 is not an error thrown by the server; it simply means no route handler matched the requested path. To handle it gracefully, place a catch-all middleware at the very bottom of your application after all defined routes:\n\n```javascript\n// Placed after all valid routes\napp.use((req, res, next) => {\n  res.status(404).json({\n    error: 'Endpoint not found',\n    requestedUrl: req.originalUrl\n  });\n});\n```",
    "question_en": "How do you handle 404 (Not Found) errors in Express?",
    "answer_en": "In Express, 404 is not an error thrown by the server; it simply means no route handler matched the requested path. To handle it gracefully, place a catch-all middleware at the very bottom of your application after all defined routes:\n\n```javascript\n// Placed after all valid routes\napp.use((req, res, next) => {\n  res.status(404).json({\n    error: 'Endpoint not found',\n    requestedUrl: req.originalUrl\n  });\n});\n```",
