    "question_hi": "What is the difference between app and Router in Express?",
    "answer_hi": "- **`app` (Application instance):** Represents the entire Express server application. It binds HTTP ports (`app.listen()`), configures global middleware, and sets app-level settings.\n- **`Router` (Mini-application):** Only capable of handling middleware and routing functions. It cannot listen on ports independently. It is used to split routes into modular sub-files (e.g., `userRouter`, `orderRouter`) and mount them onto `app`.",
