    "num": "47",
    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "What is SQL CRUD and parameterized queries?",
    "answer_hi": "SQL is used to work with data stored in a relational database like MySQL. The four basic CRUD operations are performed using SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE queries. SELECT reads data, INSERT adds new records, UPDATE changes existing records, and DELETE removes records. In Node.js, we can execute these queries using the mysql2 package. An important security rule is that we should not directly join user input into an SQL query. This can lead to SQL injection, where harmful input changes the query. Instead, we should use parameterized queries with placeholders. The database treats the supplied values as data rather than SQL commands. We should also validate user input before saving it. These practices help us build safer APIs that can create, read, update, and delete database records correctly.\n\nExample using Node.js and MySQL:\n\n```javascript\n// Read\nconst [users] = await db.execute('SELECT * FROM users');\n\n// Insert\nawait db.execute('INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)', [name, email]);\n\n// Update\nawait db.execute('UPDATE users SET name = ? WHERE id = ?', [name, id]);\n\n// Delete\nawait db.execute('DELETE FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n```\n\nRemember: Never directly join untrusted user input into an SQL query. Use placeholders such as ? and pass the values separately.",
    "question_en": "What is SQL CRUD and parameterized queries?",
    "answer_en": "SQL is used to work with data stored in a relational database like MySQL. The four basic CRUD operations are performed using SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE queries. SELECT reads data, INSERT adds new records, UPDATE changes existing records, and DELETE removes records. In Node.js, we can execute these queries using the mysql2 package. An important security rule is that we should not directly join user input into an SQL query. This can lead to SQL injection, where harmful input changes the query. Instead, we should use parameterized queries with placeholders. The database treats the supplied values as data rather than SQL commands. We should also validate user input before saving it. These practices help us build safer APIs that can create, read, update, and delete database records correctly.\n\nExample using Node.js and MySQL:\n\n```javascript\n// Read\nconst [users] = await db.execute('SELECT * FROM users');\n\n// Insert\nawait db.execute('INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)', [name, email]);\n\n// Update\nawait db.execute('UPDATE users SET name = ? WHERE id = ?', [name, id]);\n\n// Delete\nawait db.execute('DELETE FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n```\n\nRemember: Never directly join untrusted user input into an SQL query. Use placeholders such as ? and pass the values separately.",
    "source": "written",
