    "question_hi": "What is connection pooling and why is it useful?",
    "answer_hi": "A connection pool maintains a cache of active, open database connections that can be borrowed and returned by concurrent requests. Creating a new TCP and authentication handshake for every query is extremely expensive and can exhaust database connection limits. A pool recycles connections, throttles query spikes, and drastically enhances API throughput.",
