    "num": "51",
    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "What is JWT (JSON Web Token) authentication?",
    "answer_hi": "JWT stands for JSON Web Token. It is commonly used to handle authentication in web applications. First, the user sends their email and password to the login API. The server checks the credentials against the stored user data. If they are correct, the server creates a signed JWT and sends it to the client. The client sends this token with later requests to protected routes, usually through the Authorization header. The backend verifies the token before allowing access. A JWT is signed, but its contents are not automatically secret, so we should not store sensitive information inside it. We must also protect the signing secret and use HTTPS.\n\nExample:\n```javascript\nconst token = jwt.sign(\n  { id: user.id },\n  process.env.JWT_SECRET,\n  { expiresIn: '1h' }\n);\n```\n\nRemember: Login → verify credentials → create token → send token → verify token on protected routes.",
    "question_en": "What is JWT (JSON Web Token) authentication?",
    "answer_en": "JWT stands for JSON Web Token. It is commonly used to handle authentication in web applications. First, the user sends their email and password to the login API. The server checks the credentials against the stored user data. If they are correct, the server creates a signed JWT and sends it to the client. The client sends this token with later requests to protected routes, usually through the Authorization header. The backend verifies the token before allowing access. A JWT is signed, but its contents are not automatically secret, so we should not store sensitive information inside it. We must also protect the signing secret and use HTTPS.\n\nExample:\n```javascript\nconst token = jwt.sign(\n  { id: user.id },\n  process.env.JWT_SECRET,\n  { expiresIn: '1h' }\n);\n```\n\nRemember: Login → verify credentials → create token → send token → verify token on protected routes.",
    "source": "written",
    "topic": "node",
    "deep_dive": true
