    "num": "55",
    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "What is input validation and how do you do it?",
    "answer_hi": "Input validation means checking the data received from the user before processing or saving it. For example, if a user registers on a website, we should check whether the email is valid, the password is long enough, and required fields are present. Without validation, users might send incorrect or unexpected data that can cause errors or security problems. We should validate input on both the frontend and backend, but backend validation is necessary because frontend checks can be bypassed. In Express, we can check values from req.body, req.params, or req.query. For larger projects, libraries such as Joi or Zod can help us validate data consistently.\n\n```javascript\napp.post('/users', (req, res) => {\n  const { name, email } = req.body;\n\n  if (!name || !email) {\n    return res.status(400).json({\n      message: 'Name and email are required'\n    });\n  }\n\n  res.status(201).json({ message: 'Valid input' });\n});\n```\n\nRemember: Validate user input on the backend before using it.",
    "question_en": "What is input validation and how do you do it?",
    "answer_en": "Input validation means checking the data received from the user before processing or saving it. For example, if a user registers on a website, we should check whether the email is valid, the password is long enough, and required fields are present. Without validation, users might send incorrect or unexpected data that can cause errors or security problems. We should validate input on both the frontend and backend, but backend validation is necessary because frontend checks can be bypassed. In Express, we can check values from req.body, req.params, or req.query. For larger projects, libraries such as Joi or Zod can help us validate data consistently.\n\n```javascript\napp.post('/users', (req, res) => {\n  const { name, email } = req.body;\n\n  if (!name || !email) {\n    return res.status(400).json({\n      message: 'Name and email are required'\n    });\n  }\n\n  res.status(201).json({ message: 'Valid input' });\n});\n```\n\nRemember: Validate user input on the backend before using it.",
