    "num": "56",
    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "How to prevent SQL injection in Node.js?",
    "answer_hi": "SQL injection occurs when untrusted user input is directly concatenated into SQL query strings (e.g., `'SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = \"' + email + '\"'`).\n\nTo prevent it:\n1. **Use Parameterized Queries:** Always use prepared statements with placeholders (`?`) via `mysql2`. The driver escapes inputs so they are treated purely as literal data, never as executable SQL.\n2. **Avoid String Concatenation:** Never use template literals (`${}`) to embed variables directly into SQL queries.\n3. **Use an ORM/Query Builder:** Libraries like Prisma or Knex use parameterized statements by default.",
    "question_en": "How to prevent SQL injection in Node.js?",
