    "num": "57",
    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "What is CORS and how do you handle it in Express?",
    "answer_hi": "CORS stands for Cross-Origin Resource Sharing. It is a browser security mechanism that controls whether a webpage from one origin can access resources from another origin. An origin consists of the protocol, hostname, and port. For example, if our React frontend runs on localhost:5173 and our Express backend runs on localhost:5000, they have different origins. The browser may block the frontend from reading the backend's response unless the backend allows that origin through the appropriate CORS headers. In Express, we commonly use the cors package to configure this. CORS is not a replacement for authentication or authorization, and it does not prevent every type of API request.\n\nExample:\n```javascript\nconst cors = require('cors');\n\napp.use(cors({\n  origin: 'http://localhost:5173'\n}));\n```\n\nRemember: CORS controls browser-based cross-origin access. Configure allowed origins carefully instead of allowing every origin by default in production.",
    "question_en": "What is CORS and how do you handle it in Express?",
    "answer_en": "CORS stands for Cross-Origin Resource Sharing. It is a browser security mechanism that controls whether a webpage from one origin can access resources from another origin. An origin consists of the protocol, hostname, and port. For example, if our React frontend runs on localhost:5173 and our Express backend runs on localhost:5000, they have different origins. The browser may block the frontend from reading the backend's response unless the backend allows that origin through the appropriate CORS headers. In Express, we commonly use the cors package to configure this. CORS is not a replacement for authentication or authorization, and it does not prevent every type of API request.\n\nExample:\n```javascript\nconst cors = require('cors');\n\napp.use(cors({\n  origin: 'http://localhost:5173'\n}));\n```\n\nRemember: CORS controls browser-based cross-origin access. Configure allowed origins carefully instead of allowing every origin by default in production.",
