    "category": "C. Database & SQL (46–60)",
    "question_hi": "What is rate limiting and why is it important?",
    "answer_hi": "Rate limiting restricts the maximum number of requests a client (by IP or user token) can make to your server within a defined time window (e.g., 100 requests per 15 minutes).\n\nWhy it matters:\n- Protects APIs from Denial-of-Service (DoS) and Brute-Force login attacks.\n- Prevents server crashes due to runaway client loops or web scraping.\n- In Express, it is easily implemented using `express-rate-limit` middleware.",
