    "num": "82",
    "category": "E. Express Practical + Project (76–85)",
    "question_hi": "What is Postman, and how do you test an API?",
    "answer_hi": "Postman is a tool used to send HTTP requests to an API and check its responses. During backend development, we use it to test whether our endpoints work correctly, even before connecting the frontend. We can select an HTTP method such as GET, POST, PUT, or DELETE, enter the API URL, and provide headers or a JSON request body when needed. Then we check the response status code and returned data. For example, we can test a registration API by sending a POST request containing a name, email, and password. We can also test invalid input, missing fields, and unauthorized requests to check how the API handles errors. Postman helps us find bugs and verify API behavior.\n\nExample request:\n```http\nPOST http://localhost:5000/users\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"Bijay\",\n  \"email\": \"bijay@example.com\"\n}\n```\n\nRemember: Postman lets us test API requests, status codes, response data, and error cases independently of the frontend.",
    "question_en": "What is Postman, and how do you test an API?",
    "answer_en": "Postman is a tool used to send HTTP requests to an API and check its responses. During backend development, we use it to test whether our endpoints work correctly, even before connecting the frontend. We can select an HTTP method such as GET, POST, PUT, or DELETE, enter the API URL, and provide headers or a JSON request body when needed. Then we check the response status code and returned data. For example, we can test a registration API by sending a POST request containing a name, email, and password. We can also test invalid input, missing fields, and unauthorized requests to check how the API handles errors. Postman helps us find bugs and verify API behavior.\n\nExample request:\n```http\nPOST http://localhost:5000/users\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"Bijay\",\n  \"email\": \"bijay@example.com\"\n}\n```\n\nRemember: Postman lets us test API requests, status codes, response data, and error cases independently of the frontend.",
