    "category": "G. Advanced & System Architecture (101–125)",
    "question_hi": "What are the event loop phases in Node.js?",
    "answer_hi": "libuv's event loop executes in 6 specific phases per tick:\n1. **Timers:** Executes callbacks scheduled by `setTimeout()` and `setInterval()`.\n2. **Pending callbacks:** Executes I/O callbacks deferred to the next loop iteration.\n3. **Idle, prepare:** Internal use only.\n4. **Poll:** Retrieves new I/O events and executes I/O-related callbacks.\n5. **Check:** Executes `setImmediate()` callbacks.\n6. **Close callbacks:** Executes close callbacks, e.g., `socket.on('close')`.\n\nMicrotasks (`process.nextTick()` and Promise callbacks) run between each phase.",
    "question_en": "What are the event loop phases in Node.js?",
    "answer_en": "libuv's event loop executes in 6 specific phases per tick:\n1. **Timers:** Executes callbacks scheduled by `setTimeout()` and `setInterval()`.\n2. **Pending callbacks:** Executes I/O callbacks deferred to the next loop iteration.\n3. **Idle, prepare:** Internal use only.\n4. **Poll:** Retrieves new I/O events and executes I/O-related callbacks.\n5. **Check:** Executes `setImmediate()` callbacks.\n6. **Close callbacks:** Executes close callbacks, e.g., `socket.on('close')`.\n\nMicrotasks (`process.nextTick()` and Promise callbacks) run between each phase.",
    "source": "written",
    "topic": "node"
