    "question_hi": "What is middleware chaining in Express?",
    "answer_hi": "Middleware chaining is the pattern of passing a request through a sequence of discrete middleware functions before the final route handler responds. By calling `next()`, each middleware passes control to the next function in line:\n\n```javascript\napp.post('/api/posts', authMiddleware, validateBody, createPostHandler);\n```\n\nThis keeps code modular, reusable, and follows the Single Responsibility Principle.",
