    "question_hi": "What is clustering and worker_threads in Node.js?",
    "answer_hi": "- **`cluster` module:** Forks multiple instances of the Node.js process (multi-process). Each worker process has its own V8 instance, memory, and event loop, sharing the same server port. Used for scaling I/O across multi-core CPUs.\n- **`worker_threads` module:** Creates multiple threads within the **same** process, sharing memory via `ArrayBuffer` or messaging. Used for executing CPU-heavy synchronous calculations (like image processing or machine learning) without blocking the main event loop.",
    "question_en": "What is clustering and worker_threads in Node.js?",
