    "question_hi": "What are WebSockets and how do they differ from HTTP?",
    "answer_hi": "- **HTTP:** Unidirectional, stateless, request-response model. The client must initiate every request, and headers are re-sent every time.\n- **WebSocket:** Bidirectional, persistent, full-duplex TCP connection. Once an initial HTTP handshake completes, both server and client can push real-time messages to each other at any time with minimal overhead. Ideal for live chat, stock tickers, and multiplayer gaming.",
